# Minitine UI rules

[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) has the full rules. This file has the most important rules only.

## Keep the library general

Minitine is a general library. Do not put a product name, a brand or a business rule in it. Do not
put a product word in the name of a component or in the name of a prop. Put components for one
product in the application for that product.

## Use the first item that gives the result

1. A Minitine component. Examples: `AppShell`, `InspectorPanel`, `EmptyState`.
2. A Mantine component with props. Examples: `p`, `gap`, `c`, `fw`, `size`, `variant`, `radius`.
3. A Minitine token. Examples: `var(--minitine-color-border)`, `tokens.color.border`.
4. A CSS module. Use a CSS module only if props cannot give you the layout.

```tsx
// ❌ INCORRECT — a CSS module for the style of a sidebar item
<UnstyledButton className={styles.item} data-active={active}>…</UnstyledButton>

// ✅ CORRECT — the NavLink variant from the theme
<NavLink label="Board" leftSection={<Icon icon={KanbanSquare} />} active />
```

## More rules

- Do not write a color value, and do not write a `px` value in a stylesheet. Use the tokens and the
  space scale.
- Do not set a prop that the theme sets. Examples: `variant`, `radius`, `withBorder` on Card and
  Paper.
- Correct the appearance in `src/theme/mantine.ts` or in `src/assets/styles/variants.scss`. Do not
  correct it in one component.
- Use the Mantine status colors: `red`, `yellow`, `green` and `blue`.
- Give `ReactNode` props to a component. Do not write the content in the component.
- Look at each change in the light scheme and in the dark scheme.

